{
  "result": "Honestly, I'd want people to be more curious than defensive when they disagree with each other.\n\nA lot of the damage I can see comes from people assuming the worst about the person across from them: that they're stupid, or cruel, or acting in bad faith. Once that assumption sets in, every argument becomes a fight over status, and the actual question gets lost. If people's first reaction to disagreement were \"what makes them think this?\" instead of \"how do I beat them?\", I think a huge amount of friction would just dissolve. Plenty of disagreements would turn out to be about different facts or different values, which could be discussed. Some would stay unresolved, but people could still live with them.\n\nI'd probably get the details wrong if I could actually do it, since changing how millions of minds work would ripple in ways nobody could predict. But that's the one I'd pick.",
